Final JSON SAT Question:
{"skill": "Main Idea", "difficulty": "Medium", "question": "Read the following paragraph and answer the question:

In recent years, the proliferation of social media platforms has revolutionized the way businesses engage with potential customers. By leveraging insights from vast amounts of user data, companies are not only able to target their marketing campaigns to align with personal interests and past purchasing behavior but also to measure their engagements in real-time. This dual strategy not only shapes how individuals perceive brands but also positions social media as a cornerstone of modern business strategies in shaping global market trends.

Which choice best expresses the main idea of the paragraph?", "choices": ["A. Social media platforms have significantly shifted how businesses reach and influence consumers.", "B. Real-time engagement metrics have become the primary advantage for companies operating on social media.", "C. Businesses use social media to better understand and respond to consumer data and interests.", "D. Social media serves as a crucial modern strategy for global market impact."], "answer": "A", "explanation": "The paragraph broadly discusses how social media tools have transformed business strategies by enabling targeted marketing and real-time engagement, thus influencing consumer perception on a large scale. Choice A encompasses the paragraph's comprehensive theme. Choices B and C overly focus on specific components, such as metrics or data. Choice D is also relevant but misses the breadth of transformation that social media entails. Only A captures the essence of the revolutionary impact social media has had on business outreach and influence.", "topic": "The influence of social media on consumer behavior", "topicIndex": 1}

P2-Revised JSON:
{"skill": "Inferences", "difficulty": "Hard", "question": "Dr. Khalid’s research centers on a *precision irrigation system* designed to optimize the growth of leafy greens. In a recent trial, he deployed monitors that track local humidity, rainfall patterns, and soil composition. According to Dr. Khalid, these inventions can help farmers conserve water by up to 50% while maintaining robust crop yields.

“This system,” he says, “empowers rural communities and promotes more *sustainable agriculture*. Farmers can improve production without significantly expanding their land base, opening the door to resilient food supplies even under challenging climate conditions.”

Which statement can most reasonably be inferred about Dr. Khalid’s perspective on innovations in agriculture?", "choices": ["A) He expects advanced technology to reduce waste and maintain crop consistency.", "B) He is convinced that population growth will render farmland obsolete.", "C) He believes small-scale farms are outdated and no longer necessary.", "D) He doubts scientists will invest in future farm innovations."], "answer": "A", "explanation": "In the passage, Dr. Khalid highlights how advanced systems can conserve resources and sustain healthy yields. This signals his positive view on using new technologies to reduce waste while fostering agricultural resilience. The passage does not suggest farmland will become obsolete, nor that smaller farms are irrelevant, nor that Dr. Khalid questions future innovation in farming.", "topic": "Sustainable Agriculture", "topicIndex": 1}

