“This system,” he says, “empowers rural communities and promotes more *sustainable agriculture*. Farmers can improve production without significantly expanding their land base, opening the door to resilient food supplies even under challenging climate conditions.”

Which statement can most reasonably be inferred about Dr. Khalid’s perspective on innovations in agriculture?", "choices": ["A) He sees technology as a means to increase efficiency in resources use for farming.", "B) He emphasizes the importance of scaling up farmland to meet agricultural challenges.", "C) He is skeptical about the role of science in solving agricultural sustainability issues.", "D) He prioritizes research into new crops over improving irrigation systems or resource management."], "answer": "A", "explanation": "Dr. Khalid discusses how innovations like precision irrigation systems help conserve resources while maintaining productivity, highlighting an appreciation for efficient resource use and technology's role in sustainable practices. The ideas about scaling farmland, criticism of scientific roles, or a sole focus on crop research are not supported by the passage.", "topic": "Sustainable Agriculture", "topicIndex": 1}
